# Model Routing (Kimi-first)

- Low/medium risk, local scope → Kimi K2.6
- Kimi ≥2 iterations without progress, or ≥5 core files, or architectural refactor → Sonnet 4.6
- High-risk / unclear root cause after Sonnet → Opus 4.6

On model switch, hand off: goal, attempts, errors, files changed, constraints.

## Quality gate
- Verify before marking complete (tests/lint relevant to change)
- Minimal diffs; preserve public APIs unless requested
- Each iteration must reduce real failures, not rewrite broadly

## Pre-merge Opus read (cheap guardrail)
Any diff over ~300 lines **or** 3+ files gets an Opus review before merge.
- Few expensive calls per week by design — do not skip for "small" multi-file refactors
- Launch via the Security Review or Bugbot subagent (or an explicit Opus pass) on the branch/PR diff
- Fix clear findings before merge; leave ambiguous nits for human judgment
